<p>Spirit Airlines stopped operating on May 2, canceled all flights and began an immediate wind-down after last-minute rescue talks with creditors and the White House collapsed. The shutdown abruptly ended one of America’s largest low-cost airlines. The collapse followed Spirit’s bankruptcy proceedings and failed discussions over a federal rescue plan that reports described as about $500 million. Spirit and U.S. officials cited surging jet fuel costs tied to the Iran war as a key pressure, while sources also pointed to longer-running debt and competition in low-cost fares.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/3g6iHN2bI50rDrVvoFFkt1jL3kh2MPEMFyhrKzTc4Xzojh1YIvA1cSmrWQT92k9w6AHvRJoSGB_ddI4WWE2CjYMGz75LGK6bRAMg9cKVALi9' alt='A JetBlue plane taxis past grounded Spirit Airlines aircraft in Fort Lauderdale, Florida, after Spirit canceled all flights and began winding down.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Jobs at risk: The carrier’s collapse leaves roughly 17,000 workers facing possible job losses, multiple reports said.</li><li>Political dispute: Transportation Secretary Sean Duffy blamed the earlier antitrust challenge to Spirit’s JetBlue merger, while Democrats cited the fuel-price surge linked to the Iran war.</li><li>Travel disruption: Reports said the shutdown affected travelers already in transit as well as passengers with future bookings.</li></ul><blockquote>One of my coworkers joked with me that I was going to have my flight canceled mid-air, and she was nearly right - Andrew Benintende</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Spirit CEO Dave Davis: Davis said a bondholder restructuring agreement would have allowed Spirit to emerge as an operating business, but the sharp, sustained rise in fuel prices left it pursuing an orderly wind-down. (<a href='https://www.koaa.com/business/company-news/spirit-airlines-closes-grounds-fleet-leaves-customers-seeking-alternatives'>KOAA</a>)</li><li>U.S. Transportation Department: Sean Duffy said after the collapse that he did not see a need for a broader budget-airline bailout, saying larger airlines had access to cash. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/after-spirit-airlines-collapse-us-transport-chief-says-no-need-for-budget-airline-bailout'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>O’Hare travelers: CBS News Chicago reported that Spirit’s Terminal 2 area at O’Hare had no employees or passengers after the shutdown, and that some travelers arrived unaware they needed to rebook. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news/spirit-airlines-ohare/'>CBS News Chicago</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/video-spirit-airlines-shuts-down-industrys-first-iran-war-casualty/'>Spirit Airlines shuts down, industry&#x27;s first Iran war casualty</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/airlines-scramble-to-help-stranded-spirit-passengers-after-budget-carrier-collapses'>Airlines scramble to help stranded Spirit passengers after budget carrier collapses</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/may/02/spirit-airlines-ceases-operations-blame'>Political blame game begins and passengers left adrift after Spirit ceases operations</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/05/02/aviation-companies-step-up-as-spirit-winds-down_6753067_4.html'>US airlines step up as Spirit winds down</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/video/050226-saturday-morning/'>5/2: Saturday Morning</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/5/2/spirit-airlines-collapses-amid-rising-fuel-costs-from-war-on-iran'>Spirit Airlines collapses amid rising fuel costs from war on Iran</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3352244/us-carrier-spirit-airlines-shuts-down-industrys-first-iran-war-casualty'>US carrier Spirit Airlines shuts